        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "61417b9b-2e62-5bdc-b5c0-dad9a2c40afa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Guiping, Hailin, Guangxi, Heilongjiang, northeast China\n- Rivers: Qian River, Yu Jiang, Xun, Xi Jiang\n- Transportation: Harbin–Mudanjiang Intercity Railway, Mudanjiang station\n\nFacts:\n- Guiping is a county-level city in eastern Guangxi, China.\n- Hailin is a county-level city in Mudanjiang prefecture-level city, Heilongjiang province, northeast China.\n- At Guiping, the Qian River is joined by the more southerly Yu Jiang to form the Xun branch of the Xi Jiang.\n- The Harbin–Mudanjiang Intercity Railway starts in Harbin and runs east via Acheng, Maoershan, Shangzhi, Weihe, Yabuli, Hengdaohezi, and Hailin to Mudanjiang station.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a475e2b4-dd18-5bd9-908f-fe47092b76bb",
        "text": "Page: Guiping. Sentence: Guiping is a county-level city in eastern Guangxi, China.\nPage: Hailin. Sentence: Hailin () is a county-level city, part of Mudanjiang prefecture-level city, Heilongjiang province, northeast China.\nPage: Qian River. Sentence: At Guiping it is joined by the more southerly Yu Jiang to form the Xun branch of the Xi Jiang.\nPage: Harbin–Mudanjiang Intercity Railway. Sentence: Starting in Harbin, it leads east to Acheng, into mountains at Maoershan, to Shangzhi, again through the mountains to the southeast, Weihe, Yabuli, Hengdaohezi, Hailin and on to the end at Mudanjiang station.",
